{
	"info": {
		"name": "15 · Saved views",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"description": "Personal saved list-views — per-user filters/sort/hidden-columns for each list page, plus the ownership isolation.\n\n**Flow.** A) full CRUD — create, get, list (with `?resource=`), rename, replace `state` wholesale, delete, 404-after-delete; B) `(resource, name)` uniqueness **409** and an explicit-null **422**; C) isolation — a second user (`viewer`) can't see the owner's view (**404**, no existence leak) and its own list excludes it; no-token **401**.\n\n**Auth model.** Per-request: `{{admin_token}}` owns the views, `{{viewer_token}}` (also holds `saved_views:*`) probes isolation, `noauth` for the 401. Self-contained — no `00-bootstrap`, no manual token.\n\n**Permissions.** `saved_views:read|create|update|delete` are held broadly (admin, owner, red_teamer, annotator, viewer) — this is a personal convenience feature, so the interesting boundary is **ownership**, not role.\n\n**Contract notes.** `state` is a fixed envelope (`order_by`/`filters`/`hidden_columns`/`search`/`limit`/`offset`) but its `filters` values + column ids are opaque to the backend; PATCH replaces `state` wholesale; `resource` is immutable.\n\n**Leftovers.** None — both views are deleted.\n\n**Verified:** 26/26 checks green end-to-end against a live stack (`make up` + `make seedlocal`)."
	},
	"auth": {
		"type": "noauth"
	},
